From 13bde6e2d1ee75baaba62308cb8d67ef487e1f14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weizhao Ouyang <o451686892@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:55:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Pre-specialize cooperative matrix shaders before MSL
 conversion

- Apply, freeze and fold specialization constants on a SPIR-V copy
  using SPIRV-Tools-opt.
- Include specialization values in shader cache matching and
  serialization, and version the cache format.
- Avoid full reflection for shaders without cooperative matrices.
- Skip redundant optimizer input validation.
- Gate cooperative matrix availability on SPIRV-Tools.
- Use RAII for compiler lifetimes and propagate conversion failures.

Signed-off-by: Weizhao Ouyang <o451686892@gmail.com>
